value.REFLECTION_MODE.0=Sky only
value.REFLECTION_MODE.1=Reference
value.REFLECTION_MODE.2=High
option.SKY_AMBIENT=Diffuse ambient brightness
option.SKY_AMBIENT.comment=Diffuse skylight brightness. Expanded range reaches very dark and deliberately bright looks; source default1.40.
option.ambientOcclusionLevel=Corner shading
option.ambientOcclusionLevel.comment=Vanilla corner AO, default and maximum 1.00; does not raise exposure.
option.WHITE_BALANCE=Subtle white balance
option.WHITE_BALANCE.comment=Zero preserves neutral foreground colour.
option.SURFACE_SATURATION=Surface saturation
option.SURFACE_SATURATION.comment=1.00 preserves vanilla saturation. Lighting, absorption and bloom still affect the final image.
option.SURFACE_DAMPNESS=Surface dampness
option.SURFACE_DAMPNESS.comment=Broad outdoor dampness; material absorption controls darkening. Reflections cover exposed faces, with no corner mask or random noise.
value.SURFACE_DAMPNESS.0.00=Dry
value.SURFACE_DAMPNESS.0.35=Subtle
value.SURFACE_DAMPNESS.0.65=Moderate
value.SURFACE_DAMPNESS.1.00=Damp (default)
value.SURFACE_DAMPNESS.1.35=Strong
value.SURFACE_DAMPNESS.1.70=Very strong
value.SURFACE_DAMPNESS.2.00=Maximum
option.LAMP_LEVEL=Lantern and block light
option.LAMP_LEVEL.comment=Diffuse local brightness and emissive pixel interiors, with adjustable subtle bloom.
option.LAMP_HEAT=Local light warmth
option.LAMP_HEAT.comment=A restrained amber bias where block lighting dominates.
option.CLOUD_AMOUNT=Overcast coverage
option.CLOUD_AMOUNT.comment=Coverage of the finite world-height volumetric cloud layer.
option.CLOUD_SPAN=Cloud band size
option.CLOUD_SPAN.comment=Size of rounded three-dimensional cloud masses, adjustable from small banks to very broad formations.
option.CLOUD_DISTORTION=Cloud shape irregularity
option.CLOUD_DISTORTION.comment=Varies the height and internal form of connected cloud volumes. Independent of small-scale erosion.
option.CLOUD_RELIEF=Cloud shade depth
option.CLOUD_RELIEF.comment=Self-shadowing and light/dark depth within genuinely three-dimensional cloud forms.
option.CLOUD_DRIFT=Slow cloud drift
option.CLOUD_DRIFT.comment=Zero freezes the world-anchored ceiling.
option.CLOUD_LAYERS=Cloud sampling
option.CLOUD_LAYERS.comment=Cloud shape, integration and self-shadow sampling. High is the reference-quality default; lower values trade detail for speed.
option.MIST_AMOUNT=Valley mist density
option.MIST_AMOUNT.comment=Outdoor mist opacity. Cave surfaces without skylight reject valley mist.
option.MIST_Y=Lower mist altitude
option.MIST_Y.comment=World Y of the principal pale horizontal mist layer.
option.MIST_THICKNESS=Mist layer thickness
option.MIST_THICKNESS.comment=Height/depth of drifting3D fog pockets and valley layers, adjustable from thin banks to deep mist.
option.MIST_CLEAR=Clear foreground range
option.MIST_CLEAR.comment=Clear range before volumetric fog begins. Default24blocks lets nearby pockets show depth while the immediate foreground remains clear.
option.MIST_DETAIL=Mist spatial variation
option.MIST_DETAIL.comment=Sampling detail for broad horizontal density patches.
option.REFLECT_LEVEL=Water reflection amount
option.REFLECT_LEVEL.comment=Scales angle-dependent dielectric reflection. 1.00 uses physical Fresnel; underwater total internal reflection stays complete.
option.REFLECTION_MODE=Scenery reflection quality
option.REFLECTION_MODE.comment=Sky fallback,32-step scenery tracing, or96-step high-quality tracing with precise hits. Hidden geometry remains a screen-space limitation.
option.REFLECT_RANGE=Scenery trace distance
option.REFLECT_RANGE.comment=Misses fade to the procedural sky, including at screen borders.
option.WATER_VISIBILITY=Water clarity
option.WATER_VISIBILITY.comment=1.70 is the default. Higher values reduce optical extinction. Actual visibility also responds to biome sediment, rain runoff and shelter.
option.WATER_EXTINCTION=Depth absorption
option.WATER_EXTINCTION.comment=Beer-Lambert absorption and sediment scattering along the refracted path. Top, sides and underwater use the same coefficients.
option.RIPPLE_HEIGHT=Ripple strength
option.RIPPLE_HEIGHT.comment=Shading normal amplitude. Water geometry remains vanilla.
option.RIPPLE_SIZE=Ripple spacing
option.RIPPLE_SIZE.comment=Scale of the four unequal spectral wave components.
option.RIPPLE_RATE=Ripple speed
option.RIPPLE_RATE.comment=Zero freezes all surface movement.
option.FACE_SHADING=Vanilla face contrast
option.FACE_SHADING.comment=Contrast of vanilla's fixed top/side/bottom weights. No realistic directional diffuse shading is added.
option.BLOOM_STRENGTH=Subtle bloom
option.BLOOM_STRENGTH.comment=Visible restrained light halos. Emissive masking protects ordinary entities and white blocks from glowing.
option.CLOUD_ALTITUDE=Physical cloud altitude
option.CLOUD_ALTITUDE.comment=World height of the cloud layer centre. Fly below, through and above it.
option.CLOUD_THICKNESS=Physical cloud thickness
option.CLOUD_THICKNESS.comment=Vertical thickness in blocks of the world-space cloud volume.
option.SKY_LEAK=Light through the sky
option.SKY_LEAK.comment=Broad daylight glow through the cloud ceiling. Sun visibility separately controls the haze-softened solar core.
option.WET_SHEEN=Wet surface sheen
option.WET_SHEEN.comment=Independent Fresnel water film on exposed block surfaces, including nonabsorbing materials. High values deliberately exaggerate sheen.
option.BLOOM_RADIUS=Bloom radius
option.BLOOM_RADIUS.comment=Restrained halo width, stable relative to image height. Bloom strength remains a separate control.
option.SUN_VISIBILITY=Sun through overcast
option.SUN_VISIBILITY.comment=Haze-softened sun and aureole behind volumetric clouds; zero hides the solar core.
option.FACE_BLEND=Vanilla face shading
option.FACE_BLEND.comment=Blend from unshaded faces to vanilla top1.0, sides0.6/0.8 and bottom0.5. Default1.00.
option.GROUND_WARMTH=Sun-warmed ground
option.GROUND_WARMTH.comment=Golden sunlight only on outward sun-facing block faces, weighted by skylight and nearby visible occluders. No brown tint on all sides.
option.WATER_DISTORTION=Water refraction distortion
option.WATER_DISTORTION.comment=1.00 uses Snell refraction in both directions at water IOR1.333. Values above1.00 exaggerate bending artistically. Zero is an unbent comparison.
option.CIRRUS_AMOUNT=High cloud detail
option.CIRRUS_AMOUNT.comment=Thin detailed cloud volume above the main rounded cloud layer.
option.CIRRUS_ALTITUDE=High cloud altitude
option.CIRRUS_ALTITUDE.comment=World altitude of the upper wispy cloud layer.

screen.WATER=Water
screen.REFLECTIONS=Reflections
screen.WAVES=Waves and refraction
screen.LIGHTING=Lighting and shadows
screen.ATMOSPHERE=Atmosphere
screen.CLOUDS=Clouds
screen.SUN=Sun and moon
screen.FOG=Fog
screen.MATERIALS=Materials and dampness
screen.POST=Colour and bloom
screen.PERFORMANCE=Performance
option.CLOUD_STYLE=Cloud style
option.CLOUD_STYLE.comment=Stratus uses rounded world-space volumes. Vanilla uses Minecraft's actual fancy cloud geometry. Off hides both.
value.CLOUD_STYLE.0=Stratus volumetric
value.CLOUD_STYLE.1=Vanilla fancy
value.CLOUD_STYLE.2=Off
option.SUN_STYLE=Sun and moon style
option.SUN_STYLE.comment=Choose the soft overcast sun or Minecraft's original textured sun and moon.
value.SUN_STYLE.0=Stratus soft sun
value.SUN_STYLE.1=Vanilla textures
option.BIOME_WATER=Environment-aware water
option.BIOME_WATER.comment=Vanilla biome tint plus smoothed sediment, humidity, temperature, rain runoff and local cave lighting. These are visual approximations, not measured sediment data.
value.BIOME_WATER.0=Off
value.BIOME_WATER.1=On
option.WATER_TURBIDITY=Suspended sediment
option.WATER_TURBIDITY.comment=Scattering from suspended particles. Swamps and rainy rivers carry more sediment; sheltered cave water rejects rain runoff.

screen.REFRACTION=Refraction
option.REFRACTION_QUALITY=Refraction edge protection
option.REFRACTION_QUALITY.comment=The original v1.3.1 screen-offset refraction uses one shoreline depth check. Higher levels add conservative checks across the offset to reject foreground shoreline leaks.
value.REFRACTION_QUALITY.0=v1.3.1 original
value.REFRACTION_QUALITY.1=Balanced
value.REFRACTION_QUALITY.2=High (default)
option.CLOUD_DENSITY=Cloud optical thickness
option.CLOUD_DENSITY.comment=Independent density of the cloud volume, from wispy to very dense. Coverage still controls the size of cloud regions.
option.CLOUD_DETAIL=Cloud edge detail
option.CLOUD_DETAIL.comment=Fine3D erosion on rounded masses. Zero keeps large forms; higher values expose more small-scale structure.
option.MIST_SCALE=Fog pocket size
option.MIST_SCALE.comment=World-space size of drifting3D fog banks. Smaller values produce more local pockets; larger values broad valley structures.
option.MIST_BREAKUP=Fog spatial variation
option.MIST_BREAKUP.comment=Zero makes smooth fog; higher values create distinct connected pockets and gaps. Shape remains anchored in3D world space.
option.MIST_LIGHT=Fog light scattering
option.MIST_LIGHT.comment=Directional sunlight scattered by fog, with internal extinction. Independent of fog density.
option.WET_DARKENING=Material absorption darkening
option.WET_DARKENING.comment=Darkening strength on absorbent soil, timber, stone, fabric and masonry. Metals/glazed surfaces have no pore darkening. Wet sheen is separate.

option.EXPOSURE=Overall exposure
option.EXPOSURE.comment=Camera brightness in stops, affecting terrain, sky, water and bloom together. +1 doubles scene light; HUD is unchanged.

option.ATMOSPHERE_QUALITY=Atmosphere quality
option.ATMOSPHERE_QUALITY.comment=Cloud and fog image quality, independent of water reflections. Balanced retains volume detail at lower rendering cost.
value.ATMOSPHERE_QUALITY.0=Fast
value.ATMOSPHERE_QUALITY.1=Balanced
value.ATMOSPHERE_QUALITY.2=High

option.WATER_RENDER_QUALITY=Water render quality
option.WATER_RENDER_QUALITY.comment=Resolution of water surface optics. Balanced uses half resolution with depth and normal aware reconstruction. Opaque terrain and submerged blocks seen directly remain full resolution.
value.WATER_RENDER_QUALITY.0=Fast
value.WATER_RENDER_QUALITY.1=Balanced
value.WATER_RENDER_QUALITY.2=Full resolution

